      "role": "user-statement-proposition",
      "declaration": true,
      "authoredByModel": true,
      "effects": "no-world-write",
      "note": "Model language: a context-free string proposition the user message puts forward, one finite clause per wire (quoted relation phrase and common nouns in the message language, normalized, or in English; closed-inventory roles with names as written; a $id role value names another clause; link lines because, so, if, unless, although, so_that, before, after, when, while name the related clause). The host links it to the lexicon; certainty asserted lowers to a turn-local fact source user used as evidence and carried in caller-owned context; hedged, supposed or reported speech (speaker) is used only conditionally. Never stored or reinforced (DS021)."
    },
